### Components

Import from `components/...`. These work as they are:

```jinja
{% from "components/icon.html" import icon %}          {{ icon("photo_camera", size="sm") }}  {# Material Symbols; sm|md|lg|xl #}
{% from "components/dropdown.html" import dropdown %}  {{ dropdown(name="status", options=[{"value": "a", "label": "A"}], selected="a", label="Status") }}
{% from "components/spinner.html" import spinner %}    {{ spinner(size="sm") }}
```

Confirmations use `hx-confirm="Delete this?"` (a styled modal, already on every page),
toasts come from `redirect_with_toast(...)` in a route, and `window.showPrompt()` asks
for text. `button`, `input`, `textarea`, `card`, `modal` and `alert` are thin starters
(`card`, `modal` and `alert` take `{% call %}` and render only what you give them), so
style buttons, fields and cards with your own named classes in `static/css/app.css`
(`.btn-primary`, `.field`, `.card`) built from your design tokens.

### Tests

```bash
feather test                                   # everything
feather test -p tests/test_photos.py           # one file
feather test -p tests/test_photos.py -- -k post  # one test (pytest args after --)
```

Create data and sign in inside one `app.app_context()`, and keep ids, not model objects,
past it (an object used after its context is closed raises `DetachedInstanceError`):

```python
from feather.testing import login_as

def test_post(app, csrf_client):
    with app.app_context():
        user = User(email="a@b.c", username="a", active=True)
        db.session.add(user); db.session.commit()
        user_id = user.id
        login_as(csrf_client, user)
    assert csrf_client.post("/photos", data={...}).status_code == 302
```

`feather generate model|service|route` writes files where you run it, so run it in
the project you are editing.

## Deployment

This project ships a Docker deployment layout. One host runs everything
under `docker compose`: Caddy terminates TLS, `web` runs gunicorn via
`feather start`, Postgres and Valkey stay on the internal network.

| File | What it is |
|------|------------|
__FEATHER_AGENTS_DEPLOY_ROWS__

```bash
cp .env.example .env          # then fill in the blanks (SECRET_KEY, DOMAIN, ...)
feather env check             # which keys config.py reads, and what is missing
feather security-check        # production settings audit (`feather start` gates on it)

docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d   # local Postgres + Valkey
./deploy/deploy.sh                               # on the server
```

